WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.360
If you're a fan of lovable goofball&nbsp;
Ryan Reynolds — and if you're not,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:06.400
you're going to want to get your funny bone&nbsp;
checked — then you've got to be psyched for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:10.160
"Free Guy," one of the most ridiculously&nbsp;
awesome-looking movies of recent years.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:12.160
Here's everything we know about the movie so far.

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:16.080
Before we dig into the juicy details,&nbsp;
let's get this out of the way:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:19.520
"Free Guy" was originally meant to&nbsp;
open wide in theaters on July 3,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:23.600
2020. Unless you've been living under a rock&nbsp;
or have been isolated for quite some time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:27.040
you probably have a pretty strong&nbsp;
inkling about why "Free Guy" was delayed.

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:29.920
For a while after being bumped from&nbsp;
its original date, it seemed like "Free&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:34.400
Guy" was locked in for a December 11, 2020&nbsp;
release date, but that didn't happen either.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:39.680
The movie's current release date, assuming nothing&nbsp;
happens to bump it again, is August 13, 2021.

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:44.240
"Free Guy" is one of the first major films to&nbsp;
be released under the new banner of 20th Century&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:49.040
Studios, the moniker bestowed upon the former&nbsp;
20th Century Fox after its acquisition by Disney.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:53.360
The House of Mouse varied its approach to its&nbsp;
releases that were originally slated for 2020.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.360 --> 00:00:57.280
While the studio pushed back the premiere dates&nbsp;
of tentpole films like the live-action "Mulan"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.280 --> 00:01:01.360
remake and Marvel's "Black Widow," it didn't&nbsp;
do so until it became clear that such a move&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:05.440
was necessary. In the case of "Free Guy," a&nbsp;
delay was certainly the best course of action,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:09.040
and the fact that the studio went so&nbsp;
far as to push it into summer 2021&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:11.840
is a strong signal that they&nbsp;
believe it will do well in theaters.

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:15.600
"Free Guy" is directed by "Night&nbsp;
at the Museum" helmer Shawn Levy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:19.120
from a screenplay by Matt Lieberman and&nbsp;
Zak Penn, a veteran scribe who has worked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.120 --> 00:01:23.120
on everything from "Men in Black" to "The&nbsp;
Avengers." Their cast is riddled with ringers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.120 --> 00:01:27.040
several of whom were cast largely due to&nbsp;
their connections to the video game world.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.040 --> 00:01:31.040
Popping up in supporting roles or cameos&nbsp;
will be YouTuber Tyler "Ninja" Blevins,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.040 --> 00:01:35.360
Twitch star Imane "Pokimane" Anys, Let's&nbsp;
Play favorite Lannan "LazarBeam" Eacott,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:40.400
and Sean "Jacksepticeye" McLoughlin, who will be&nbsp;
voicing the iconic video game character Q*Bert.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:44.320
Since that character speaks nearly exclusively&nbsp;
in bleeped curses, this should be interesting.

00:01:46.320 --> 00:01:50.720
"What's he saying, Felix?" "Stand&nbsp;
by. My Q-bertese is a little rusty."

00:01:50.720 --> 00:01:55.200
The familiar faces don't end there. Appearing in&nbsp;
the main cast are "Thor: Ragnarok" director Taika&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.200 --> 00:02:00.080
Waititi as video game developer Antoine, "Killing&nbsp;
Eve's" Jodie Comer as programmer Milly and her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.080 --> 00:02:04.800
in-game alter ego Molotov Girl, "Stranger&nbsp;
Things' star Joe Keery as programmer Keys,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:09.120
and "Get Out" actor Lil Rel Howery as&nbsp;
Guy's fellow NPC and friend, Buddy.

00:02:09.120 --> 00:02:13.600
One thing we're extremely curious about is&nbsp;
who or what will serve as the in-game Big Bad.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:17.280
While Guy will be working against external&nbsp;
forces to keep his world from collapsing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:20.640
it stands to reason that he'll have some&nbsp;
kind of virtual nemesis to contend with,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:24.400
as well. But as far as who or what that&nbsp;
villain could be, we still don't know.

00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:29.760
The story of "Free Guy" has had a long road&nbsp;
to theaters, even before the pandemic delays.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:34.640
Deadline reported back in 2016 that the film —&nbsp;
back then, described as a Matt Lieberman spec&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.640 --> 00:02:38.480
script "in the vein of 'The Truman Show'" — had&nbsp;
acquired the highly sought-after "Deadpool" star&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.480 --> 00:02:42.160
Ryan Reynolds. The overall plot seems&nbsp;
to have remained the same since then,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:46.080
but given Reynolds' star power, and his love&nbsp;
of getting creatively involved in his projects,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:49.840
it's likely that the movie's tone evolved from&nbsp;
there to match his personality and talents.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:53.360
And while Reynolds wasn't one of&nbsp;
the initial creators of the project,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.360 --> 00:02:57.600
it's clear that he fell deeply in&nbsp;
love with it: in 2019, he said,

00:02:57.600 --> 00:03:01.600
"I haven't been this fully immersed and engaged&nbsp;
in something since 'Deadpool' [...] I think we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:05.680
live in really weird times right now, you're&nbsp;
watching the news and the top story today is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.680 --> 00:03:09.520
'it's the end of the world.' I felt a kinship&nbsp;
to the character in that you can sometimes feel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.520 --> 00:03:14.000
like a background character. The world is on loop&nbsp;
and you have no control over what's happening."

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:16.560
That sounds like a fascinating&nbsp;
theme to explore through comedy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:21.600
and we're intrigued to see how "Free Guy" tackles&nbsp;
the idea of an NPC facing an existential crisis.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:25.600
But beyond the broad themes and premise, we&nbsp;
actually don't know much about the movie's plot,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:28.480
although the trailers give us&nbsp;
a good idea of what to expect.

00:03:28.480 --> 00:03:33.520
The first trailer is, simply put, gloriously&nbsp;
bonkers. Set to the bouncy strains of Mariah&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:36.800
Carey's "Fantasy," it shows a look&nbsp;
at a typical day in Guy's life.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.800 --> 00:03:40.480
That leads to his snap decision to suddenly&nbsp;
involve himself in the mayhem that results in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.480 --> 00:03:44.880
his world turning upside-down, and his reaction&nbsp;
to his realization that his world isn't exactly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.880 --> 00:03:48.800
you know, real. We also get an idea of&nbsp;
the excellent comedic chemistry between&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.800 --> 00:03:53.360
Reynolds and Comer, along with an abundance&nbsp;
of explosions, gunfights, and wild stunts.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.360 --> 00:03:57.520
It's not like Ryan Reynolds has a conflicted&nbsp;
history when it comes to those sort of things....

00:03:57.520 --> 00:04:01.360
"Answer as quickly as you can now.&nbsp;
If you had a gun to your head..."

00:04:06.640 --> 00:04:10.880
The second trailer for "Free Guy" is just as&nbsp;
jam-packed with awesomeness as its predecessor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.880 --> 00:04:14.240
but offers a more concrete sense&nbsp;
of the movie's narrative. Guy is a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.240 --> 00:04:17.200
background character of a video&nbsp;
game who learns he isn't real,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:20.880
then ventures to become the hero of his&nbsp;
world and save it from impending doom.

00:04:20.880 --> 00:04:24.400
The third trailer places further emphasis&nbsp;
on the character of Molotov Girl,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:27.440
and the role she plays in the plot.&nbsp;
It seems she will be instrumental in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.440 --> 00:04:31.040
Guy's development from clueless&nbsp;
NPC to self-aware action hero.

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:34.000
Of course, although there's a lot&nbsp;
we can figure out from the trailers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:38.000
there's a lot more we don't know. In addition&nbsp;
to our questions about the movie's main villain,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:42.160
we also wonder just how Jodie Comer's dual&nbsp;
character will figure in. She's been presented&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.160 --> 00:04:46.720
as an in-game ally to Guy, but she is also one&nbsp;
of the game's programmers in the real world.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.720 --> 00:04:50.240
With this in mind, it sure seems like she&nbsp;
could have a key role to play in convincing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.240 --> 00:04:53.600
Taika Waititi's developer character&nbsp;
not to pull the plug on the game.

00:04:53.600 --> 00:04:58.080
But beyond Guy's gradual evolution into a hero,&nbsp;
the details of the story of "Free Guy" remains a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.080 --> 00:05:02.080
mystery. That's probably a good thing, as we feel&nbsp;
like this is going to be a flick that's full of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.080 --> 00:05:07.600
hilarious and inspired surprises. Most likely, the&nbsp;
less you know, the more enjoyable it will all be.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.600 --> 00:05:11.040
And based on the trailers so far, we&nbsp;
have a solid idea of its overall vibe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:13.520
which is every bit as hilarious&nbsp;
as you would hope for it to be.

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:16.080
"That's not Huge Jackman though."

00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:19.440
"It sure isn't that's like&nbsp;
5'9" Wolvie from the comics."

00:05:19.440 --> 00:05:22.400
"Yeah that's like real Wolverine.&nbsp;
Hugh Jackman outdid himself."

00:05:22.400 --> 00:05:23.360
"Never heard of him." -

00:05:23.360 --> 00:05:27.040
Considering the video game-themed plot,&nbsp;
including a number of game references,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:27.040 --> 00:05:29.200
cameos, and more, it goes without saying that if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.200 --> 00:05:32.560
there's a prime audience for "Free&nbsp;
Guy," it's the gaming community.

00:05:32.560 --> 00:05:35.600
"There's so many callbacks to&nbsp;
the games we know and love.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.600 --> 00:05:37.760
You're going to be really excited to see it."

00:05:37.760 --> 00:05:40.240
However, Ryan Reynolds has&nbsp;
fans all over the place,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.240 --> 00:05:44.320
some of whom may have never even held a&nbsp;
game controller. Will these people get lost?

00:05:44.320 --> 00:05:48.080
Not according to Reynolds. During a&nbsp;
2019 press conference, Reynolds drew&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.080 --> 00:05:52.160
a comparison to sports movies, and how even&nbsp;
people who might have no interest in, say,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:52.160 --> 00:05:56.800
an actual baseball game can still be&nbsp;
thrilled by a baseball movie. In his words,

00:05:56.800 --> 00:06:00.800
"I always look at it like, sports movies are&nbsp;
good metaphors. The greatest sports movies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.800 --> 00:06:04.560
ever made are not actually about sports.&nbsp;
'Field of Dreams,' I wouldn't characterize&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:04.560 --> 00:06:08.720
that as a baseball story. They used baseball&nbsp;
as a vehicle to tell a really beautiful story&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.720 --> 00:06:12.480
about a son and a father trying to connect.&nbsp;
I think that we're doing the same thing."

00:06:12.480 --> 00:06:16.320
Director Shawn Levy added that the movie's&nbsp;
central conceit about an NPC who is just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.320 --> 00:06:20.960
finding out that he's in a game means that the&nbsp;
ideal audience surrogate is actually a non-gamer.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.960 --> 00:06:24.000
A non-gaming audience will easily&nbsp;
be able to place themselves in Guy's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:27.200
shoes as he learns all about what&nbsp;
video games are, and how they work.

00:06:27.200 --> 00:06:31.280
So while gamers will be thrilled with all the&nbsp;
inside jokes and fun twists on things they love,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:31.280 --> 00:06:35.200
the whole high-concept premise is really&nbsp;
just there to tell a more universal story.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:35.200 --> 00:06:38.960
And honestly, if audiences could&nbsp;
figure out "The Matrix" back in 1999,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:38.960 --> 00:06:40.960
they should be more than ready for "Free Guy."

00:06:41.760 --> 00:06:45.440
Not that long ago, there wouldn't even be a&nbsp;
question about whether a major studio release&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.440 --> 00:06:49.200
would play in theaters or not. Things&nbsp;
have changed a lot since 2020, though,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.200 --> 00:06:52.880
and these days, there's always some question&nbsp;
about whether a movie will release in theaters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:52.880 --> 00:06:56.400
or if it'll go right to streaming — or,&nbsp;
in some cases, if it'll go up on both&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:56.400 --> 00:06:59.520
simultaneously. So where does it fall&nbsp;
in this new entertainment landscape?

00:06:59.520 --> 00:07:03.120
In fact, it looks like "Free Guy" is taking&nbsp;
full advantage of the reopening of theaters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.120 --> 00:07:06.960
nationwide thanks to increasing vaccination&nbsp;
rates and lowering COVID restrictions.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:07.520 --> 00:07:10.000
In fact, just like in the pre-COVID era "Free Guy"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:13.840
will release exclusively in theaters&nbsp;
for the first 45 days of its run.

00:07:13.840 --> 00:07:17.920
This is in contrast to some of Disney's other&nbsp;
big releases such as "Cruella" and "Black&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:17.920 --> 00:07:22.960
Widow," which debuted in theaters and on Disney+&nbsp;
simultaneously. But it looks like Disney's release&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.960 --> 00:07:27.120
strategy is beginning to shift. "Free Guy"&nbsp;
comes out in August, just a few weeks ahead&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:27.120 --> 00:07:31.280
of the studio's next big release, "Shang-Chi&nbsp;
and the Legend of the Ten Rings." Clearly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:31.280 --> 00:07:36.080
Disney is banking on earning big bucks with this&nbsp;
movie, and on theaters coming back in a big way.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:36.080 --> 00:07:39.920
Given the enthusiasm that "Free Guy" has earned&nbsp;
all over the internet so far and public's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:39.920 --> 00:07:43.680
excitement to return to movie theaters,&nbsp;
this seems like a good bet on their part.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:43.680 --> 00:07:48.160
We'll see if their plan pays off when "Free&nbsp;
Guy" hits theaters on August 13, 2021.

